# Print arguments that fail, at today's baseline. Print is one N-ary
# invocation (PIR plan §3): after Step 6, an argument failure that no closer
# || resolves suppresses the complete invocation and its newline.
#
# What each case does after Step 6:
#   - every unhandled OOB case here emits no line (today it materializes and
#     prints a zero);
#   - the failed-conditional case keeps today's whole-line suppression — that
#     is retained language behavior, not a change;
#   - ranged OOB iterations emit no line, in-bounds iterations still print;
#   - a fallback resolves before the invocation boundary and lets the
#     complete line print;
#   - empty strings are successful values, so their line always prints and
#     stays distinguishable from an invocation suppressed by failure.
#
# Still to add when Step 6 lands: leak checks on the suppressed path, where
# arguments (including successful siblings) own heap temporaries.

arr = [10 20 30]
arr2 = [40 50]
v1 = 5
v2 = 6

"--oob first--"
arr[9], v1, v2

"--oob middle--"
v1, arr[9], v2

"--oob last--"
v1, v2, arr[9]

"--double oob middle--"
v1, arr[9], arr2[9], v2

"--oob beside owned heap temp--"
"s" ⊕ "t", arr[9], v1

"--empty args always print--"
v1, "", "", v2

"--ranged checked--"
j = 0:5
v1, arr[j]

"--cond middle--"
k = 0:5
v1, (k > 3) + 0, v2

"--end--"
